-- title:
--   Igusa-branch prolongation traces to the Gauss reduction at level M'
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and `coeffMap`, `coeffEmb` denote the coefficientwise maps between Laurent series fields.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** $q$ is a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; $\kappa_A$ denotes its residue field. $W$ is a finite set of places of $C_{M'} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` (the intermediate field of $\kappa_A((q))$ generated over $\kappa_A$ by `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold expansion `jqNModC`) over $\kappa_A$, a place being a proper valuation subring containing $\kappa_A$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring; the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`, that is of the places $w$ which are rational ($\kappa_A$ surjects onto the residue field of $w$), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ_A M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ_A`. An element $s$ of $W$ is fixed.
--
--   **Function fields.** $\bar F_{M'} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$, and $\bar F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` is the corresponding base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\bar F_{M'} \le \bar F$, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` is the resulting embedding.
--
--   **The constant reduction $R_0$ and its Gauss property.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A ↥\bar F_{M'} C_{M'}`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\bar F_{M'}$, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto $C_{M'}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of that subring, which restricts to $A$ on the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and is compatible with the residue map of $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of functions with nonzero residue, and the normalisation that every nonzero $f$ can be scaled by a constant so as to have nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that image belongs to `R₀.integers` and its `R₀.residue`, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$; so $R_0$ is the coefficientwise, or Gauss, reduction.
--
--   **Uniqueness of the Gauss ring (`hGU`).** Writing $\hat\jmath$ for the element of $\bar F_{M'}$ obtained from `jq` by the coefficient embedding, the hypothesis `hGU` requires: every valuation subring $V$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ which (i) induces exactly $A$ on constants ($a \in A$ if and only if the image of $a$ lies in $V$, for all $a \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$), (ii) contains $\hat\jmath$, and (iii) has $\hat\jmath$ residually transcendental in the sense that for every polynomial $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(\hat\jmath)$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $V$ and in its maximal ideal, has the same elements as `R₀.integers`.
--
--   **Local data over a subfield $k_0$.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has its image in $A$; put $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$. The hypotheses require that $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ be a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), that its residue field be algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Equipping $\bar F$ with the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, the assertion is the following, for all further data as listed.
--
--   Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \bar F$ such that the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$, and such that the following independence condition holds: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar F$ whose members all lie in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ inducing exactly $A$ on $k_0$ (for $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$), which is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$.
--
--   Let $O$ be a Noetherian local subring of $F_0$ with $O \subseteq W_0$, inducing exactly $A$ on $k_0$, such that every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ by a non-unit of $O$, and such that $F_0$ is the fraction field of $O$ (every $f \in F_0$ satisfies $fh = g$ for some $g, h \in O$ with $h \neq 0$).
--
--   Let $E_0 \ge 1$, let the image of $\pi_0$ lie in $O$, let $cx, cy \in O$, let $u$ be a unit of $O$, let $\hat A_0$ be the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, let $\mathcal U$ be the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A_0\,\pi^{E_0}$, i.e. $\hat A_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ modulo the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{E_0}$ with $\pi$ the image of $\pi_0$, let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathcal U$, and let $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ be units of $\mathcal U$, subject to: $cx\,cy = \pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image in the completion of every constant coming from an $x \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$ in $\hat A_0$; $\iota$ of the image of $cx$ equals $\gamma_U \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U`, and $\iota$ of the image of $cy$ equals $\gamma_V \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V`; $cy$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and $cx$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, does not lie in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   Let $W_x$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ with $O \subseteq W_x$, inducing exactly $A$ on $k_0$, which is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, and for which some $t \in W_x$ is residually transcendental in the sense that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal then each coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal. At $W_x$ the roles of $cx$ and $cy$ are exchanged with respect to $W_0$: $cx$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, and $cy$ does not. Finally $W_x$ is required to satisfy the following branch law: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficient-embedded image $\hat g \in \bar F_{M'}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, and which is such that $\hat g$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\hat\jmath$ has non-negative order, the image of $\hat g$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $F_0$; that element lies in $W_x$; it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when `R₀.residue` of $\hat g$ is $0$; and if `R₀.residue` of $\hat g$ lies in the valuation subring of the chosen supersingular place $s$, then that element lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and having image in $O$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals `s.evalAt` of `R₀.residue` of $\hat g$, the difference of the two elements of $O$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   Under all of these hypotheses: for every field $FI$ carrying a $\kappa_A$-algebra structure and every `RegularProlongation A ↥\bar F FI` $R_x$ — a valuation subring `Rx.integers` of $\bar F$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $FI$ with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and with the scaling normalisation — such that `Rx.integers` induces $W_x$ on $F_0$ (for $f \in F_0$, the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in `Rx.integers` if and only if $f \in W_x$), the conclusion is that for every $f \in \bar F_{M'}$ the image `IntermediateField.inclusion hle f` lies in `Rx.integers` if and only if $f$ lies in `R₀.integers`; that is, the trace of $R_x$ on the level-$M'$ field is exactly the Gauss reduction ring $R_0$.
--
--   This is the sharp integrality statement for the Igusa-side branch in the semistable reduction of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at the prime $q$: the prolongation along that branch restricts on the level-$M'$ modular function field to the Gauss (constant) reduction, no smaller and no larger. It is used in the construction of a branch place of the Igusa component lying over the fixed supersingular place, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch_of_prime).
